;; Every model and data artifact the voice extension installs. `assets.clj` is the
;; only reader.
;;
;; Sources, tried in the order `assets/sources` returns:
;;   :hf        Hugging Face; first when a token is configured, skipped when not
;;              (`:is-token-required true`). Credentials never cross the redirect
;;              to HF's CDN.
;;   :pack      the Vis voice assets release - only what Vis exports itself or may
;;              mirror outright. No voice and no GPL data.
;;   :upstream  the publisher: the fallback, and the only source of anything Vis
;;              does not host.
;; Every source of one entry delivers the same bytes, so one `:sha256` covers all.
;;
;; `:needs-espeak-ng true` - silent until espeak-ng's phoneme tables are ON THE
;; SYSTEM. Vis does not ship them: GPL-3.0-or-later, one package away, read from
;; their own directory at run time, and shared by every Piper voice.
;;
;; `:is-commercial-ok true` is the bar for anything Vis MIRRORS or fetches by
;; itself. An entry that fails it is listed with `:is-opt-in true`: never in the
;; pack, refused by `assets/ensure!`, fetched only when a user names it.
